{"name":"Salal Leaves","hex":"#637d74","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"salal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A leathery-leaved North American shrub, Gaultheria shallon, with edible sepals and leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salal"},{"term":"leaves","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of leaf","from leave:\nplural of leave \nplural of leave"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of leave"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leaves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gaultheria shallon","blocks":[{"text":"Gaultheria shallon is an evergreen shrub in the heather family (Ericaceae), native to western North America. Common names include salal, shallon, or gaultheria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gaultheria_shallon_RF.jpg/330px-Gaultheria_shallon_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaultheria_shallon"},{"title":"Leaf","blocks":[{"text":"A leaf is a principal appendage of the stem of a vascular plant, usually borne laterally above ground and specialized for photosynthesis. Leaves are collectively called foliage, as in \"autumn foliage\", while the leaves, stem, flower, and fruit collectively form the shoot system. In most leaves, the primary photosynthetic tissue is the palisade mesophyll and is located on the upper side of the blade or lamina of the leaf, but in some species, including the mature foliage of Eucalyptus, palisade mesophyll is present on both sides and the leaves are said to be isobilateral. The leaf is an integral part of the stem system, and most leaves are flattened and have distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surfaces that differ in color, hairiness, the number of stomata, the amount and structure of epicuticular wax, and other features. Leaves are mostly green in color due to the presence of a compound called chlorophyll, which is essential for photosynthesis as it absorbs light energy from the Sun. A leaf with lighter-colored or white patches or edges is called a variegated leaf."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lisc_lipy.jpg/330px-Lisc_lipy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaf"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Gaultheria_shallon_31974.JPG/500px-Gaultheria_shallon_31974.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Gaultheria_shallon_31974.JPG/1280px-Gaultheria_shallon_31974.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Gaultheria_shallon_31974.JPG/500px-Gaultheria_shallon_31974.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The finely and sharply serrate leaves are shiny and dark green above.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGaultheria_shallon_31974.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Salal_berries.jpg/500px-Salal_berries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Salal_berries.jpg/1280px-Salal_berries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Salal_berries.jpg/500px-Salal_berries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ripe berries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalal_berries.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png/500px-Leaf_Varieties_%2815_sp%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: